WEBVTT

00:00:08.452 --> 00:00:10.484
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:10.522 --> 00:00:11.378
Sammy!

00:00:12.117 --> 00:00:14.088
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:14.111 --> 00:00:14.674
Go!

00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:19.601
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:20.208 --> 00:00:21.686
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:25.521 --> 00:00:28.923
This is dad's book. I think dad
wants us to pick up where he left off.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.876
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:30.891 --> 00:00:33.519
Family business. Do you think
Mom wanted all this for us?

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:34.645
I can't do this alone.

00:00:35.412 --> 00:00:36.163
I'm driving.

00:01:08.547 --> 00:01:10.416
Man, these are some phat houses, huh?

00:01:10.792 --> 00:01:11.923
I'd like to live here.

00:01:12.261 --> 00:01:12.599
Yeah.

00:01:13.162 --> 00:01:14.708
Too bad you can't afford it.

00:01:15.662 --> 00:01:16.837
Yeah, you're right.

00:01:17.512 --> 00:01:19.850
This neighborhood will be
damn expensive when it's done.

00:01:44.628 --> 00:01:45.899
This place is perfect...

00:01:46.475 --> 00:01:46.903
Ow!

00:01:48.097 --> 00:01:49.283
...Except for the mosquitoes.

00:01:53.349 --> 00:01:54.100
Aah!

00:01:55.264 --> 00:01:55.744
Dustin?

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:58.183
Help me, I'm trapped!

00:01:59.135 --> 00:02:00.416
I broke my ankle.

00:02:01.969 --> 00:02:02.991
I'll get a rope!

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:06.537
Oh, damn.

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:24.664
Oh god!

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:36.749
Travis, help!

00:02:36.911 --> 00:02:37.710
Hang on!

00:02:48.035 --> 00:02:49.513
Travis, help!

00:02:49.973 --> 00:02:51.775
Aah! Aaah!

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:53.525
It's okay, Dustin. It's okay.

00:02:56.964 --> 00:02:57.517
Dustin?

00:02:59.030 --> 00:02:59.907
Dustin, I'm here.

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:02.945
Oh, god.

00:03:10.868 --> 00:03:12.603
<i>I got something to say.</i>

00:03:29.221 --> 00:03:29.936
<i>Ow!</i>

00:03:32.452 --> 00:03:33.648
<i>Yeah, you're doing all right.</i>

00:03:33.664 --> 00:03:35.282
<i>Gonna start a fire</i>

00:03:38.558 --> 00:03:40.478
You know, we could get
day jobs once in a while.

00:03:41.342 --> 00:03:42.468
Hunting's our day job,

00:03:42.984 --> 00:03:44.110
And the pay is crap.

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:45.518
Yeah, but hustling pool,

00:03:46.254 --> 00:03:47.158
Credit-Card scams?

00:03:47.842 --> 00:03:49.513
It's not the most honest
thing in the world, Dean.

00:03:49.743 --> 00:03:50.804
Well, let's see... Honest...

00:03:51.795 --> 00:03:52.506
Fun and easy...

00:03:53.964 --> 00:03:54.879
It's no contest.

00:03:55.075 --> 00:03:55.484
Besides,

00:03:56.055 --> 00:03:57.404
We're good at it. It's
what we were raised to do.

00:03:57.473 --> 00:04:00.284
How we were raised was
jacked. Yeah, says you.

00:04:00.717 --> 00:04:02.328
We got a new gig or what? Maybe.

00:04:02.568 --> 00:04:05.203
Oasis Plains, Oklahoma.
Not far from here.

00:04:05.498 --> 00:04:06.856
Gas-Company employee.

00:04:07.626 --> 00:04:09.362
Dustin Burwash,

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.907
Supposedly died from creutzfeldt-Jakob.

00:04:12.244 --> 00:04:12.584
Huh?

00:04:13.229 --> 00:04:15.399
Human mad cow disease. Mad cow?

00:04:16.525 --> 00:04:17.856
Wasn't that on "Oprah"?

00:04:18.402 --> 00:04:19.428
You watch "Oprah"?

00:04:22.713 --> 00:04:25.531
So this guy eats a bad burger.
Why is it our kind of thing?

00:04:26.748 --> 00:04:29.528
Mad cow disease causes
massive brain degeneration.

00:04:29.531 --> 00:04:31.998
It takes months, even years
for the damage to appear,

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:33.188
But this guy, Dustin,

00:04:33.376 --> 00:04:35.994
Sounds like his brain
disintegrated in about an hour,

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.258
Maybe less.

00:04:37.275 --> 00:04:38.748
Okay, that's weird. Yeah.

00:04:39.217 --> 00:04:40.523
Now, it could be a disease,

00:04:41.184 --> 00:04:42.710
Or it could be something much nastier.

00:04:43.658 --> 00:04:45.301
All right, Oklahoma.

00:04:45.947 --> 00:04:47.429
Man, work, work, work.

00:04:48.339 --> 00:04:49.733
No time to spend my money.

00:04:50.862 --> 00:04:54.770
<i>We got the power, we got the glory</i>

00:04:54.954 --> 00:04:57.020
<i>Just say you need it...</i>

00:05:04.851 --> 00:05:05.802
Travis Weaver?

00:05:07.561 --> 00:05:08.358
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:09.715 --> 00:05:11.756
Are you the Travis who
worked with uncle Dusty?

00:05:12.776 --> 00:05:14.489
Dustin never mentioned nephews.

00:05:15.052 --> 00:05:15.650
Really?

00:05:16.108 --> 00:05:17.316
Well, he sure mentioned you.

00:05:17.363 --> 00:05:18.829
He said you were the greatest.

00:05:19.275 --> 00:05:20.037
Oh, he did?

00:05:20.525 --> 00:05:21.182
Huh.

00:05:21.898 --> 00:05:23.681
So, we wanted to ask you...

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.417
What exactly happened out there?

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:27.693
I'm not sure.

00:05:28.168 --> 00:05:30.866
He fell in the sinkhole. I went
to the truck to get some rope, and

00:05:31.382 --> 00:05:32.696
By the time I got back...

00:05:33.412 --> 00:05:34.620
What'd you see?

00:05:36.145 --> 00:05:36.591
Nothing.

00:05:37.313 --> 00:05:38.052
Just Dustin.

00:05:38.134 --> 00:05:39.870
No wounds or anything?

00:05:40.316 --> 00:05:41.231
Well, he was bleeding

00:05:41.442 --> 00:05:43.846
From his eyes and his ears, his nose,

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:45.242
That's it.

00:05:45.876 --> 00:05:47.670
So do you think it could
be this whole mad cow thing?

00:05:49.366 --> 00:05:50.035
I don't know.

00:05:50.645 --> 00:05:51.853
That's what the doctors are saying.

00:05:51.923 --> 00:05:52.827
But if it was,

00:05:53.472 --> 00:05:57.824
He would have acted strange beforehand,
like dementia, loss of motor control.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.821
You ever notice anything like that? No.

00:06:00.199 --> 00:06:00.752
No way.

00:06:02.002 --> 00:06:04.316
Yeah, but if it wasn't some
disease, what the hell was it?

00:06:05.517 --> 00:06:06.395
That's a good question.

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:06.972
Yep.

00:06:07.182 --> 00:06:08.595
Can you tell us where this happened?

00:06:09.361 --> 00:06:09.751
Yeah.

00:06:33.568 --> 00:06:34.024
Huh.

00:06:35.575 --> 00:06:36.296
What do you think?

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:38.002
I don't know,

00:06:38.017 --> 00:06:40.607
But if that guy Travis was right,
it happened pretty damn fast.

00:06:41.389 --> 00:06:42.200
So what?

00:06:42.523 --> 00:06:44.175
Some sort of creature
chewed on his brain?

00:06:44.198 --> 00:06:45.625
No, there'd be an entry wound.

00:06:46.046 --> 00:06:47.744
Sounds like this thing
worked from the inside.

00:06:51.579 --> 00:06:52.105
Huh.

00:06:53.232 --> 00:06:55.088
It looks like there's only room for one.

00:06:55.899 --> 00:06:56.966
You want to flip a coin?

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:00.240
Dean, we have no idea what's down there.

00:07:01.773 --> 00:07:03.268
All right, I'll go if you're scared.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:04.551
Scared?

00:07:04.956 --> 00:07:06.068
Flip the damn coin.

00:07:09.767 --> 00:07:10.563
Call it in the air...

00:07:10.826 --> 00:07:11.405
Chicken.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:14.034
I'm going.

00:07:14.102 --> 00:07:15.011
I said I'd go.

00:07:15.324 --> 00:07:16.333
I'm going.

00:07:16.752 --> 00:07:17.600
All right.

00:07:19.509 --> 00:07:20.858
Don't drop me.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.107
So, you found some beetles

00:07:27.212 --> 00:07:28.550
In a hole in the ground.

00:07:29.429 --> 00:07:30.860
That's shocking, Sam.

00:07:31.388 --> 00:07:33.429
There were no tunnels, no tracks,

00:07:33.852 --> 00:07:36.385
No evidence of any other
kind of creature down there.

00:07:36.635 --> 00:07:38.386
You know, some beetles do eat meat.

00:07:38.405 --> 00:07:41.192
Now, it's usually dead meat, but...
How many did you find down there?

00:07:41.464 --> 00:07:41.924
10.

00:07:43.365 --> 00:07:45.730
It would take a whole lot more than
that to eat out somebody's brain.

00:07:45.843 --> 00:07:47.063
Well, maybe there were more.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:49.502
I don't know. It sounds
like a stretch to me.

00:07:49.524 --> 00:07:52.362
We need more information on
the area, the neighborhood,

00:07:52.386 --> 00:07:55.025
Whether something like this
has ever happened before.

00:07:57.007 --> 00:07:57.524
What?

00:07:58.239 --> 00:07:59.588
I know a good place to start.

00:08:01.154 --> 00:08:03.429
I'm kind of hungry for a
little barbecue, how about you?

00:08:06.045 --> 00:08:07.652
What, we can't talk to the locals?

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:10.874
And the free food's got nothing to do
with it? Of course not. I'm a professional.

00:08:11.456 --> 00:08:11.953
Right.

00:08:31.913 --> 00:08:34.491
Growing up in a place like
this would freak me out.

00:08:35.157 --> 00:08:35.795
Why?

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:40.362
The manicured lawns, the"how
was your day, honey?"...

00:08:40.462 --> 00:08:41.940
I'd blow my brains out.

00:08:43.395 --> 00:08:45.213
There's nothing wrong with normal.

00:08:46.445 --> 00:08:48.380
I'd take our family over normal any day.

00:08:52.598 --> 00:08:54.440
Welcome. Is this the barbecue?

00:08:54.534 --> 00:08:56.774
Yeah, not the best weather, but...

00:08:56.962 --> 00:09:00.704
I'm Larry Pike, the developer here,
and you are? Dean. This is Sam.

00:09:00.968 --> 00:09:02.563
Sam, Dean, good to meet you.

00:09:02.974 --> 00:09:05.578
So, you two are interested
in Oasis Plains? Yes, sir.

00:09:06.106 --> 00:09:06.962
Let me just say

00:09:07.068 --> 00:09:10.552
That we accept homeowners of
any race,religion, color, or...

00:09:11.122 --> 00:09:12.448
Sexual orientation.

00:09:14.078 --> 00:09:15.099
We're brothers.

00:09:15.881 --> 00:09:19.729
Our father is getting on in years, and
we're just looking for a place for him.

00:09:19.823 --> 00:09:20.409
Great,

00:09:20.597 --> 00:09:22.720
Great. Well, seniors are
welcome, too. Come on in.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:28.889
You said you were the developer?

00:09:29.088 --> 00:09:31.975
18 months ago, I was walking
this valley with my survey team.

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:35.098
There was nothing here but
scrub brush and squirrels,

00:09:35.296 --> 00:09:37.914
And you know what? We built
such a nice place to live

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:40.607
That I actually bought into
it myself. This is our house.

00:09:40.776 --> 00:09:45.012
We're the first family in Oasis
Plains. This is my wife, Joanie.

00:09:45.088 --> 00:09:45.951
Hi, there. Hi,

00:09:45.998 --> 00:09:47.556
Nice to meet you. Sam and Dean.

00:09:47.717 --> 00:09:49.031
Sam. Joannie.

00:09:49.087 --> 00:09:50.814
Tell them how much you
love the place, honey.

00:09:51.217 --> 00:09:54.141
And lie if you have to because
I need to sell some houses.

00:09:55.258 --> 00:09:56.694
Boys, if you'll excuse me.

00:09:57.548 --> 00:10:01.104
Don't let his salesman routine scare
you. This really is a great place to live.

00:10:01.246 --> 00:10:03.132
Hi, I'm Linda Bloom, head of sales.

00:10:03.226 --> 00:10:04.868
And Linda was second to move in.

00:10:04.981 --> 00:10:06.764
She's a very noisy neighbor, though.

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:09.835
She's kidding, of course.

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:12.716
I take it you two are interested
in becoming homeowners.

00:10:13.421 --> 00:10:14.650
Well... Y-Yeah.

00:10:14.653 --> 00:10:19.859
Well, let me just say that we accept
homeowners of any race, religion, color,or...

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:22.252
Sexual orientation.

00:10:22.615 --> 00:10:23.108
Hmm.

00:10:23.272 --> 00:10:23.976
Right.

00:10:24.351 --> 00:10:26.463
Uh, I'm gonna go talk to Larry.

00:10:26.791 --> 00:10:27.659
Okay, honey?

00:10:33.317 --> 00:10:34.877
You have three choices...

00:10:34.995 --> 00:10:37.047
Carpet, hardwood, and tile.

00:10:37.118 --> 00:10:37.845
Whoa,

00:10:38.514 --> 00:10:39.886
Someone likes bugs.

00:10:40.508 --> 00:10:43.523
My son. He's into insects.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:45.758
He's very inquisitive.

00:10:46.509 --> 00:10:47.130
Hmm.

00:10:47.283 --> 00:10:50.509
Who can say no to a steam
shower? I use mine every day.

00:10:50.919 --> 00:10:51.940
Sounds great.

00:10:52.075 --> 00:10:55.336
You also have three different
whirlpool tubs to choose from.

00:10:55.343 --> 00:10:57.522
The hardware for the tubs
include nickel, brass,

00:10:57.574 --> 00:11:00.557
And when you see the kitchens,
you can choose from... Excuse me.

00:11:00.602 --> 00:11:02.021
Um, okay.

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:15.371
Is this yours?

00:11:15.694 --> 00:11:17.351
You gonna tell my dad? I don't know.

00:11:17.541 --> 00:11:18.483
Who's your dad?

00:11:19.188 --> 00:11:19.873
Yeah.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:22.610
Larry usually skips me in
the family introductions.

00:11:22.715 --> 00:11:26.281
Ouch. First-Name basis with the
old man... sounds pretty grim.

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:28.252
Well, I'm not exactly brochure material.

00:11:28.572 --> 00:11:30.924
Well, hang in there. It gets
better. Alright? I promise.

00:11:31.458 --> 00:11:32.068
When?

00:11:32.091 --> 00:11:32.713
Matthew!

00:11:41.869 --> 00:11:44.215
I am so sorry about my son and his...

00:11:44.344 --> 00:11:45.834
Pet. It's no bother.

00:11:46.338 --> 00:11:47.394
Excuse us.

00:11:54.612 --> 00:11:55.785
Remind you of somebody?

00:12:00.536 --> 00:12:01.169
Dad?

00:12:02.654 --> 00:12:03.980
Dad never treated us like that.

00:12:04.766 --> 00:12:06.854
Well, dad never treated you
like that. You were perfect.

00:12:06.865 --> 00:12:08.343
He was all over my case.

00:12:10.098 --> 00:12:11.283
You don't remember?

00:12:12.162 --> 00:12:14.555
Maybe he had to raise his voice,
but sometimes you were out of line.

00:12:14.572 --> 00:12:15.294
Right.

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:19.177
Right, like when I said I'd rather
play soccer than learn bow hunting.

00:12:19.371 --> 00:12:20.920
Bow hunting's an important skill.

00:12:22.057 --> 00:12:22.796
Whatever.

00:12:24.181 --> 00:12:25.917
How was your tour?

00:12:26.104 --> 00:12:28.110
It was excellent.I'm ready to buy.

00:12:28.305 --> 00:12:30.112
So you might be onto something.

00:12:30.745 --> 00:12:33.443
Looks like Dustin Burwash wasn't
the first strange death around here.

00:12:33.607 --> 00:12:34.205
What happened?

00:12:34.362 --> 00:12:36.212
About a year ago,
before they broke ground,

00:12:36.272 --> 00:12:38.511
One of Larry's surveyors
dropped dead while on the job.

00:12:38.859 --> 00:12:41.436
Get this... severe allergic
reaction to bee stings.

00:12:41.752 --> 00:12:42.984
More bugs. More bugs.

00:12:45.547 --> 00:12:47.912
I've heard of killer
bees, but killer beetles?

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:49.996
What is it that could
make different bugs attack?

00:12:51.761 --> 00:12:54.683
Well, hauntings sometimes
include bug manifestations.

00:12:54.718 --> 00:12:57.199
Yeah, but I didn't see any
evidence of ghost activity.

00:12:57.349 --> 00:12:58.449
Yeah, me neither.

00:13:00.247 --> 00:13:03.394
Maybe they're being controlled
somehow... by something or someone.

00:13:03.929 --> 00:13:05.172
You mean like "Willard"?

00:13:05.206 --> 00:13:06.792
Yeah, bugs instead of rats.

00:13:08.316 --> 00:13:13.844
There are cases of psychic connections between
people and animals, elementals, telepaths.

00:13:13.856 --> 00:13:15.944
Yeah, that whole Timmy/Lassie thing.

00:13:17.254 --> 00:13:18.532
Larry's kid...

00:13:19.107 --> 00:13:20.362
Bugs for pets.

00:13:20.831 --> 00:13:21.981
Matt? Yeah.

00:13:23.784 --> 00:13:27.186
He did try to scare the realtor with
a tarantula. Think he's our willard?

00:13:27.373 --> 00:13:28.288
I don't know.

00:13:28.347 --> 00:13:29.989
Anything's possible, I guess.

00:13:32.167 --> 00:13:34.055
Ooh, hey, pull over here.

00:13:42.918 --> 00:13:44.314
What are we doing here?

00:13:48.185 --> 00:13:49.768
It's too late to talk to anybody else.

00:13:51.701 --> 00:13:54.117
We're gonna squat in an empty house?

00:13:54.739 --> 00:13:56.693
I want to try the steam shower. Come on.

00:13:57.608 --> 00:13:58.476
Come on!

00:14:26.133 --> 00:14:29.440
Atoko valley county began
mandatory insecticide

00:14:29.478 --> 00:14:32.209
Spraying across a wide
swath of the district today.

00:14:32.249 --> 00:14:37.982
Authorities say the decision to spray was made
because of several recent cases of west nile virus,

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:42.489
Coupled with a dramatic increase in
the mosquito population in some areas.

00:14:42.809 --> 00:14:47.292
Although some residents cite concerns about
the high levels of pesticide being used...

00:15:12.525 --> 00:15:15.763
Aaah! Aaah!

00:15:45.331 --> 00:15:46.570
You ever coming out of there?

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:47.640
What?!

00:15:47.912 --> 00:15:50.887
Dean, a police call came
in on the scanner. Hold on.

00:15:50.929 --> 00:15:53.800
Someone was found dead three
blocks from here. Come on.

00:15:56.364 --> 00:15:57.838
This shower is awesome.

00:15:58.072 --> 00:15:58.948
Come on.

00:16:27.188 --> 00:16:29.328
Okay, look, I don't know
anything more right now.

00:16:29.375 --> 00:16:30.989
I'll have to call you back.

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:31.843
All right.

00:16:33.251 --> 00:16:34.978
Hello, you're back early.

00:16:34.996 --> 00:16:38.609
Yeah, we wanted to take another look
at the neighborhood. What's going on?

00:16:40.855 --> 00:16:44.308
You guys met Linda
Bloom at the barbecue?

00:16:44.486 --> 00:16:45.322
The realtor.

00:16:45.903 --> 00:16:46.936
Well, she, uh,

00:16:47.831 --> 00:16:49.041
Passed away last night.

00:16:50.496 --> 00:16:51.190
What happened?

00:16:52.553 --> 00:16:53.839
I'm still trying to find out.

00:16:54.402 --> 00:16:56.204
I identified the body for the police.

00:16:57.733 --> 00:16:59.460
I'm sorry. This isn't a good time.

00:16:59.724 --> 00:17:00.325
It's okay.

00:17:00.484 --> 00:17:01.357
Excuse me.

00:17:04.747 --> 00:17:06.052
You know what we have to do, right?

00:17:07.196 --> 00:17:09.786
We got to get in that house.
See if we got a bug problem.

00:17:37.382 --> 00:17:38.902
This looks like the place.

00:17:52.576 --> 00:17:53.468
Spiders.

00:17:54.189 --> 00:17:55.374
From spider boy?

00:17:55.562 --> 00:17:56.312
Matt.

00:17:58.119 --> 00:17:58.905
Maybe.

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:23.633
Isn't his house that way?

00:18:23.692 --> 00:18:24.642
Yep.

00:18:28.149 --> 00:18:29.663
So where's he going?

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:56.545
Hey, Matt.

00:18:57.355 --> 00:18:58.364
Remember me?

00:18:59.321 --> 00:19:00.294
What are you doing out here?

00:19:00.412 --> 00:19:01.784
We want to talk to you.

00:19:03.368 --> 00:19:04.916
You're not here to buy a house, are you?

00:19:05.956 --> 00:19:06.718
Wait,

00:19:07.539 --> 00:19:08.830
You're not serial killers?

00:19:09.182 --> 00:19:11.281
No, no. No, I think you're safe.

00:19:12.618 --> 00:19:13.651
So, Matt...

00:19:14.798 --> 00:19:16.639
You sure know a lot about insects.

00:19:17.765 --> 00:19:18.340
So?

00:19:19.534 --> 00:19:21.681
Did you hear what happened
to Linda, the realtor?

00:19:23.499 --> 00:19:24.871
I hear she died this morning.

00:19:25.054 --> 00:19:26.133
Mm, that's right.

00:19:26.497 --> 00:19:27.740
Spider bites.

00:19:28.608 --> 00:19:29.359
Matt,

00:19:30.227 --> 00:19:32.526
You tried to scare her with a spider.

00:19:34.153 --> 00:19:34.751
Wait,

00:19:35.443 --> 00:19:36.874
You think I had
something to do with that?

00:19:37.461 --> 00:19:38.528
You tell us.

00:19:39.326 --> 00:19:41.320
That tarantula was a joke.

00:19:41.918 --> 00:19:45.408
Anyway, that wouldn't explain the
bee attack or the gas-Company guy.

00:19:46.768 --> 00:19:48.071
You know about those?

00:19:48.505 --> 00:19:49.877
There is something going on here.

00:19:50.346 --> 00:19:51.437
I don't know what,

00:19:51.539 --> 00:19:52.020
But

00:19:52.443 --> 00:19:54.261
Something's happening with the insects.

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:56.008
Let me show you something.

00:20:03.856 --> 00:20:06.858
So, if you knew about all this
bug stuff, why not tell your dad?

00:20:06.964 --> 00:20:08.794
Maybe he could clear everybody out.

00:20:08.958 --> 00:20:10.671
Believe me, I've tried, but

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:12.701
Larry doesn't listen to me.

00:20:12.947 --> 00:20:13.604
Why not?

00:20:13.956 --> 00:20:14.941
Mostly?

00:20:15.082 --> 00:20:17.065
He's too disappointed in his freak son.

00:20:18.836 --> 00:20:19.751
I hear ya.

00:20:20.428 --> 00:20:21.202
You do?

00:20:23.501 --> 00:20:24.662
Matt, how old are you?

00:20:24.733 --> 00:20:25.530
16.

00:20:26.868 --> 00:20:29.624
Well, don't sweat it 'cause in two
years something great's gonna happen.

00:20:30.304 --> 00:20:31.617
What? College.

00:20:32.110 --> 00:20:34.714
You'll be able to get out of
that house and away from your dad.

00:20:35.301 --> 00:20:37.802
What kind of advice is that? A
kid should stick with his family.

00:20:42.928 --> 00:20:43.961
How much further, Matt?

00:20:44.133 --> 00:20:45.141
We're close.

00:21:06.465 --> 00:21:08.671
I've been keeping track of
the insect population. It's

00:21:08.893 --> 00:21:10.653
Part of an A.P. Science class.

00:21:12.002 --> 00:21:13.269
You two are like peas in a pod.

00:21:15.331 --> 00:21:16.257
What's been happening?

00:21:16.492 --> 00:21:17.313
A lot.

00:21:18.005 --> 00:21:20.527
I mean, from bees to earthworms,

00:21:20.957 --> 00:21:22.083
Beetles...

00:21:22.212 --> 00:21:23.690
You name it. It's

00:21:23.748 --> 00:21:25.543
Like they're congregating here.

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:26.259
Why?

00:21:26.775 --> 00:21:27.701
I don't know.

00:21:30.326 --> 00:21:31.112
What's that?

00:22:07.937 --> 00:22:09.122
There's something down there.

00:22:15.808 --> 00:22:17.181
Oh, come on.

00:23:07.632 --> 00:23:10.385
So, a bunch of skeletons
in an unmarked grave.

00:23:10.502 --> 00:23:12.473
Yeah, maybe this is a haunting...

00:23:12.602 --> 00:23:13.904
Some pissed-Off spirits,

00:23:14.244 --> 00:23:16.542
Some unfinished business. Yeah, maybe.

00:23:16.624 --> 00:23:18.583
The question is, why bugs

00:23:18.700 --> 00:23:19.768
And why now?

00:23:20.225 --> 00:23:21.703
That's two questions.

00:23:23.029 --> 00:23:24.648
So, with that kid back there...

00:23:24.984 --> 00:23:27.471
How could you tell him to just
ditch his family like that?

00:23:27.682 --> 00:23:28.879
Just, uh,

00:23:29.278 --> 00:23:30.943
I know what the kid's going through.

00:23:31.267 --> 00:23:34.751
How about telling him to respect his old
man? How's that for advice? Dean, come on.

00:23:35.455 --> 00:23:37.132
This isn't about his old man.

00:23:37.214 --> 00:23:38.517
You think I didn't respect dad.

00:23:38.634 --> 00:23:39.854
That's what this is about.

00:23:40.998 --> 00:23:42.464
Just forget it. Sorry I brought it up.

00:23:42.523 --> 00:23:43.555
I respected him,

00:23:44.318 --> 00:23:45.702
But no matter what I did,

00:23:45.948 --> 00:23:47.192
It was never good enough.

00:23:47.309 --> 00:23:49.972
What are you saying, that dad
was disappointed in you? Was?

00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:52.153
Is...

00:23:52.623 --> 00:23:54.757
Always has been. Why
would you think that?

00:23:54.804 --> 00:23:56.540
Because I didn't want to bow hunt

00:23:56.709 --> 00:23:59.653
Or hustle pool, because I wanted
to go to school and live my life,

00:23:59.668 --> 00:24:02.052
Which in our whacked-Out
family made me the freak.

00:24:04.127 --> 00:24:06.461
Yeah, you were kind of like the
blond chick in "the munsters."

00:24:07.799 --> 00:24:08.444
Dean,

00:24:09.183 --> 00:24:11.728
You know what most dads are when
their kids score a full ride?

00:24:12.702 --> 00:24:13.417
Proud.

00:24:14.919 --> 00:24:17.112
Most dads don't toss their
kids out of the house.

00:24:18.457 --> 00:24:19.712
I remember that fight.

00:24:20.779 --> 00:24:23.536
In fact, I seem to recall a few choice
phrases coming out of your mouth.

00:24:28.339 --> 00:24:29.114
You know,

00:24:29.630 --> 00:24:32.316
Truth is, when we finally do find dad,

00:24:33.243 --> 00:24:35.272
I don't know if he's
even gonna want to see me.

00:24:37.055 --> 00:24:39.056
Sam, dad was never disappointed in you.

00:24:40.288 --> 00:24:40.980
Never.

00:24:42.247 --> 00:24:43.432
He was scared.

00:24:44.155 --> 00:24:45.328
What are you talking about?

00:24:45.375 --> 00:24:48.038
He was afraid of what could have
happened to you if he wasn't around.

00:24:49.563 --> 00:24:51.263
But even when you two weren't talking,

00:24:52.104 --> 00:24:54.345
He used to swing by
Stanford whenever he could,

00:24:55.107 --> 00:24:56.057
Keep an eye on you,

00:24:56.796 --> 00:24:58.087
Make sure you were safe.

00:24:58.779 --> 00:24:59.717
What?

00:25:01.133 --> 00:25:01.778
Yeah.

00:25:05.943 --> 00:25:07.585
Why didn't he tell me any of that?

00:25:09.549 --> 00:25:12.118
It's a two-Way street, dude. You
could have picked up the phone.

00:25:17.901 --> 00:25:19.736
Come on, we're gonna be
late for our appointment.

00:25:28.053 --> 00:25:29.566
So, you two are students?

00:25:29.991 --> 00:25:31.058
Yeah.

00:25:31.164 --> 00:25:33.416
Yeah, we're in your class.

00:25:33.663 --> 00:25:34.965
Anthro 101.

00:25:35.363 --> 00:25:36.525
Oh, yeah.

00:25:36.595 --> 00:25:37.369
So,

00:25:37.440 --> 00:25:39.410
What about the bones, Professor?

00:25:40.288 --> 00:25:43.045
This is quite an
interesting find you've made.

00:25:43.092 --> 00:25:47.139
I'd say they're 170
years old, give or take.

00:25:47.725 --> 00:25:49.555
The time frame and the geography

00:25:49.574 --> 00:25:51.498
Heavily suggest native american.

00:25:51.944 --> 00:25:55.281
Were there any tribes or
reservations on that land?

00:25:55.363 --> 00:25:58.061
Not according to the historical record,

00:25:58.132 --> 00:25:59.059
But

00:25:59.493 --> 00:26:00.701
The, uh...

00:26:00.748 --> 00:26:04.889
Relocation of native peoples
was quite common at that time.

00:26:05.135 --> 00:26:05.874
Right.

00:26:06.678 --> 00:26:07.312
Well,

00:26:07.828 --> 00:26:09.364
Are there any local legends,

00:26:09.576 --> 00:26:11.793
Oral histories about the area?

00:26:12.778 --> 00:26:13.963
Well...

00:26:14.573 --> 00:26:18.139
You know, there's a
euchee tribe in Sapulpa.

00:26:18.369 --> 00:26:20.128
It's about 60 miles from here.

00:26:21.536 --> 00:26:23.503
Someone out there might know the truth.

00:26:26.612 --> 00:26:27.644
All right.

00:27:14.038 --> 00:27:15.242
Joe Whitetree?

00:27:16.968 --> 00:27:19.983
We'd like to ask you a few
questions, if that's all right.

00:27:20.587 --> 00:27:22.124
We're students from the university.

00:27:22.182 --> 00:27:24.235
No, you're not. You're lying.

00:27:26.276 --> 00:27:27.074
Um,

00:27:27.672 --> 00:27:30.464
The truth is... You know
who starts sentence with

00:27:30.589 --> 00:27:31.669
"Truth is"?

00:27:32.067 --> 00:27:33.064
Liars.

00:27:37.963 --> 00:27:39.722
Have you heard of Oasis Plains?

00:27:39.769 --> 00:27:42.232
It's a housing development
near the Atoka valley.

00:27:44.948 --> 00:27:45.969
I like him.

00:27:46.661 --> 00:27:47.893
He's not a liar.

00:27:48.984 --> 00:27:50.157
I know the area.

00:27:51.541 --> 00:27:53.535
What can you tell us
about the history there?

00:27:53.672 --> 00:27:54.775
Why do you want to know?

00:27:55.444 --> 00:27:56.687
Something...

00:27:57.086 --> 00:27:58.153
Something bad

00:27:59.021 --> 00:28:00.992
Is happening in Oasis Plains.

00:28:01.959 --> 00:28:05.654
We think it might have something to do
with some old bones we found down there...

00:28:06.863 --> 00:28:08.329
Native american bones.

00:28:13.192 --> 00:28:15.503
I'll tell you what my
grandfather told me,

00:28:16.265 --> 00:28:18.107
What his grandfather told him.

00:28:18.857 --> 00:28:20.335
200 years ago,

00:28:20.602 --> 00:28:23.335
A band of my ancestors
lived in that valley.

00:28:24.086 --> 00:28:27.687
One day, the american
calvary came to relocate them.

00:28:30.770 --> 00:28:32.365
They were resistant...

00:28:32.999 --> 00:28:34.665
Calvary impatient.

00:28:36.248 --> 00:28:38.019
As my grandfather put it,

00:28:39.052 --> 00:28:39.887
On a night,

00:28:40.016 --> 00:28:41.060
The moon

00:28:41.388 --> 00:28:42.350
And the sun

00:28:42.631 --> 00:28:44.872
Shared the sky as equals,

00:28:46.162 --> 00:28:48.848
The calvary first raided our village.

00:28:49.466 --> 00:28:50.499
They murdered,

00:28:51.202 --> 00:28:52.035
Raped.

00:28:53.114 --> 00:28:55.470
The next day, the calvary came again,

00:28:55.752 --> 00:28:57.851
And the next and the next.

00:28:58.250 --> 00:29:01.347
And on the sixth night, the
calvary came one last time,

00:29:02.492 --> 00:29:04.510
And by the time the sun rose,

00:29:04.686 --> 00:29:06.820
Every man, woman, and child

00:29:06.891 --> 00:29:08.624
Still in the village

00:29:08.976 --> 00:29:10.008
Was dead.

00:29:14.625 --> 00:29:16.455
They say on the sixth night,

00:29:16.608 --> 00:29:19.212
As the chief of the village lay dying,

00:29:19.564 --> 00:29:21.440
He whispered to the heavens

00:29:22.285 --> 00:29:25.616
That no white man would
ever tarnish this land again.

00:29:26.536 --> 00:29:27.545
Nature

00:29:27.920 --> 00:29:29.105
Would rise up

00:29:29.773 --> 00:29:31.357
And protect the valley,

00:29:31.521 --> 00:29:34.606
And it would bring as many
days of misery and death

00:29:35.177 --> 00:29:36.326
To the white man

00:29:36.983 --> 00:29:39.106
As the calvary had
brought upon his people.

00:29:40.901 --> 00:29:41.992
Insects.

00:29:42.880 --> 00:29:44.299
That sounds like nature to me.

00:29:45.848 --> 00:29:46.915
Six days?

00:29:47.185 --> 00:29:49.285
And on the night of the sixth day,

00:29:50.183 --> 00:29:51.814
None would survive.

00:30:00.243 --> 00:30:02.155
When did the gas-Company man die?

00:30:03.140 --> 00:30:05.744
Let's see, we got here
tuesday, so friday the 20th.

00:30:06.265 --> 00:30:07.168
March 20th.

00:30:08.118 --> 00:30:09.549
That's the spring equinox.

00:30:10.253 --> 00:30:12.611
The night, the sun and the
moon share the sky as equals.

00:30:12.707 --> 00:30:16.542
So every year about this time,
anybody in Oasis Plains is in danger.

00:30:17.211 --> 00:30:20.796
Larry built his neighborhood on cursed land.
And on the sixth night... that's tonight.

00:30:21.125 --> 00:30:24.550
If we don't do something, Larry's
family will be dead by sunrise.

00:30:25.895 --> 00:30:27.303
So how do we break a curse?

00:30:27.631 --> 00:30:28.769
You don't break a curse.

00:30:29.168 --> 00:30:31.350
You get out of its way. We got
to get those people out now.

00:31:49.564 --> 00:31:52.579
Yes, mr. Pike, there's a main-Line
gas leak in your neighborhood.

00:31:52.661 --> 00:31:54.209
God, really? And how big?

00:31:54.315 --> 00:31:57.060
Well, it's fairly extensive.
I don't want to alarm you, but

00:31:57.189 --> 00:32:01.001
We need your family out of the vicinity for
at least 12 hours or so, just to be safe.

00:32:01.139 --> 00:32:02.148
And who is this again?

00:32:02.207 --> 00:32:04.940
Travis Weaver. I work for
Oklahoma gas and power.

00:32:04.987 --> 00:32:05.561
Uh-Huh.

00:32:05.770 --> 00:32:09.606
The problemis I know Travis. He's worked
with us for a year. So who is this?

00:32:10.134 --> 00:32:11.152
Uh...

00:32:12.842 --> 00:32:13.886
Give me the phone.

00:32:22.876 --> 00:32:23.509
Hello?

00:32:23.626 --> 00:32:24.623
Matt, it's Sam.

00:32:24.905 --> 00:32:26.907
Sam, my backyard's
crawling with cockroaches.

00:32:26.908 --> 00:32:30.356
Matt, just listen. You have to get your
family out of that house right now, okay?

00:32:30.648 --> 00:32:31.502
What, why?

00:32:32.390 --> 00:32:33.639
Because something's coming.

00:32:34.296 --> 00:32:35.132
More bugs.

00:32:35.480 --> 00:32:36.738
Yeah, a lot more.

00:32:37.828 --> 00:32:39.922
My dad doesn't listen in
the best of circumstances.

00:32:39.942 --> 00:32:42.889
What am I supposed to tell him?
You got to make him listen, okay?

00:32:43.088 --> 00:32:44.321
Give me the phone. Give me the phone!

00:32:44.532 --> 00:32:47.679
Matt, under no circumstances are you to
tell the truth. He'll just think you're nuts.

00:32:47.808 --> 00:32:50.332
But he's my... Tell him you have
a sharp pain in your right side,

00:32:50.391 --> 00:32:51.952
And you got to go to the hospital, okay?

00:32:52.083 --> 00:32:53.774
Yeah. Yeah, okay.

00:32:57.625 --> 00:32:58.658
"Make him listen."

00:32:59.362 --> 00:33:00.454
What are you thinking?

00:33:12.495 --> 00:33:14.126
Damn it, they're still here. Come on.

00:33:21.957 --> 00:33:24.137
Get off my property
before I call the cops!

00:33:24.184 --> 00:33:25.863
Mr. Pike, listen. Dad,

00:33:26.368 --> 00:33:27.389
They're just trying to help.

00:33:27.436 --> 00:33:28.493
Get in the house!

00:33:29.044 --> 00:33:30.712
Sorry. I told him the truth.

00:33:30.770 --> 00:33:32.602
We had a plan, Matt.
What happened to the plan?

00:33:33.412 --> 00:33:35.020
Look, it's twelve a.M.

00:33:35.161 --> 00:33:36.558
They are coming any minute now.

00:33:36.617 --> 00:33:39.704
You need to get your family
and go before it's too late.

00:33:39.835 --> 00:33:41.830
Oh, yeah, you mean
before the biblical swarm.

00:33:42.006 --> 00:33:44.437
What do you think really
happened to that realtor, huh?

00:33:44.578 --> 00:33:45.975
And the gas-Company guy?

00:33:46.421 --> 00:33:48.240
You don't think something
weird's going on around here?

00:33:48.360 --> 00:33:50.673
Look, I don't know who
you are, but you're crazy.

00:33:50.686 --> 00:33:53.146
You come near my boy or my family again,

00:33:53.243 --> 00:33:54.318
We're gonna have a problem.

00:33:54.363 --> 00:33:57.037
Well, I hate to be a downer, but we got
a problem right now. Dad, they're right.

00:33:57.256 --> 00:33:58.188
We're in danger.

00:33:59.150 --> 00:34:01.163
Matt, get inside now!

00:34:01.539 --> 00:34:02.583
Why won't you listen to me?!

00:34:02.673 --> 00:34:05.043
Because this is crazy!
It doesn't make any sense!

00:34:05.366 --> 00:34:05.900
Look,

00:34:06.160 --> 00:34:07.768
This land is cursed.

00:34:08.106 --> 00:34:11.510
People have died here. Are you gonna
really take that risk with your family?

00:34:11.522 --> 00:34:12.033
Wait.

00:34:14.212 --> 00:34:14.926
You hear it?

00:34:19.346 --> 00:34:20.405
What the hell?

00:34:25.011 --> 00:34:27.077
It's time to go. Larry, get your wife.

00:34:27.798 --> 00:34:28.219
Guys.

00:34:32.447 --> 00:34:33.536
Oh, my god.

00:34:35.616 --> 00:34:36.826
We'll never make it.

00:34:36.878 --> 00:34:38.854
Everybody in the house.
Everybody in the house!

00:34:39.070 --> 00:34:39.739
Let's go!

00:34:44.678 --> 00:34:46.858
Is there anyone else in the
neighborhood? No, it's just us.

00:34:47.497 --> 00:34:48.699
Honey, what's happening?

00:34:49.259 --> 00:34:50.303
What's that noise?

00:34:51.468 --> 00:34:52.437
Call 911.

00:34:53.256 --> 00:34:54.133
Joanie!

00:34:54.389 --> 00:34:55.020
Okay.

00:34:56.275 --> 00:34:57.870
I need towels.

00:34:57.982 --> 00:35:01.242
We got to lock this place up. Come on, doors,
windows, the fireplace, everything. Okay?

00:35:01.941 --> 00:35:02.954
Phones are dead.

00:35:03.035 --> 00:35:04.393
They must have chewed
through the phone lines.

00:35:10.563 --> 00:35:11.597
And the power lines.

00:35:11.838 --> 00:35:12.691
Maybe my cell.

00:35:16.004 --> 00:35:16.946
No signal.

00:35:17.513 --> 00:35:18.487
You won't get one.

00:35:19.220 --> 00:35:20.880
They're blanketing the house.

00:35:37.897 --> 00:35:38.955
So, what do we do now?

00:35:39.682 --> 00:35:40.673
We try to outlast it.

00:35:42.711 --> 00:35:45.469
Hopefully the curse will
end at sunrise. Hopefully?

00:36:08.485 --> 00:36:10.270
Bug spray? Trust me.

00:36:13.229 --> 00:36:13.776
What is that?

00:36:24.281 --> 00:36:25.161
The flue.

00:36:27.975 --> 00:36:29.748
I think everybody needs to get upstairs.

00:36:40.968 --> 00:36:43.226
Everybody upstairs now! Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:36:46.607 --> 00:36:47.956
Quick!

00:36:56.763 --> 00:36:59.248
Okay, Joanie, go, go, go.

00:36:59.285 --> 00:37:00.236
Matt, go.

00:37:01.797 --> 00:37:02.888
Hurry!

00:37:09.666 --> 00:37:10.652
You in? Yeah.

00:37:13.812 --> 00:37:15.574
Come on!

00:37:22.185 --> 00:37:23.582
My god, what's that?!

00:37:29.915 --> 00:37:31.161
Something's eating through the wood.

00:37:32.587 --> 00:37:33.428
Termites.

00:37:37.870 --> 00:37:39.259
All right, everybody get back.

00:37:39.414 --> 00:37:40.856
Get back! Get back!

00:37:40.886 --> 00:37:41.456
Get back!

00:37:42.530 --> 00:37:43.318
Matt.

00:38:45.099 --> 00:38:47.492
Huddle together. Cover your faces.

00:38:58.252 --> 00:38:59.015
Look!

00:40:00.382 --> 00:40:01.328
What, no goodbye?

00:40:01.853 --> 00:40:02.694
Good timing.

00:40:02.807 --> 00:40:04.278
Another hour and we'd have been gone.

00:40:04.834 --> 00:40:05.449
For good?

00:40:06.388 --> 00:40:06.998
Yeah.

00:40:07.051 --> 00:40:10.820
The development's been put on hold while the
government investigates those bones you found,

00:40:11.255 --> 00:40:12.644
But I'm gonna make damn sure

00:40:12.774 --> 00:40:13.908
No one lives here again.

00:40:14.704 --> 00:40:16.152
You don't seem too upset about it.

00:40:17.385 --> 00:40:20.621
Well, this has been the biggest
financial disaster of my career, but,

00:40:22.047 --> 00:40:23.158
Somehow...

00:40:25.059 --> 00:40:26.366
I really don't care.

00:40:41.651 --> 00:40:42.560
What's this?

00:40:42.792 --> 00:40:43.618
I don't know.

00:40:44.827 --> 00:40:45.510
They

00:40:45.788 --> 00:40:47.109
Kind of weird me out now.

00:40:49.690 --> 00:40:51.090
Yeah, I should hope so.

00:41:12.116 --> 00:41:13.197
I want to find dad.

00:41:15.004 --> 00:41:15.807
Yeah, me too.

00:41:17.421 --> 00:41:18.525
Yeah, but I just...

00:41:21.915 --> 00:41:23.341
I want to apologize to him.

00:41:26.884 --> 00:41:27.508
For what?

00:41:30.082 --> 00:41:31.793
All the things I said to him.

00:41:34.651 --> 00:41:36.115
He was just doing the best he could.

00:41:39.483 --> 00:41:41.090
Well, don't worry, we'll find him,

00:41:42.298 --> 00:41:43.752
And you'll apologize,

00:41:44.573 --> 00:41:47.196
And within five minutes, you guys
will beat each other's throats.

00:41:51.274 --> 00:41:53.116
Yeah, probably.

00:41:55.872 --> 00:41:57.444
Let's hit the road. Let's.



